  "text_pages": [
    "Mobility in exchange programs - International Welcome e-desk - University of Strasbourg\nShare the page :\nAdd the page to your favorites :\nPage has been added to favorites\nPage has been removed from favorites\nMobility in exchange programs\nErasmus+ mobility\nErasmus is the leading exchange program for European students!\nIt allows students to spend 2 to 12 months in one of 33 partner countries, including France, while continuing to earn credits at their home university.\nInter-university agreements\nThe University of Strasbourg offers international students the opportunity to study there under cooperation agreements, networks, or virtually.\nMobility within the Epicur alliance\nThe European EPICUR alliance (European Partnership for an Innovative Campus Unifying Regions), launched in 2019, brings together nine universities from seven different countries. Led by the University of Strasbourg, it offers student and teacher mobility, assistance in developing joint training programs and innovative projects with a European dimension.\nMobility within Eucor - The European Campus\nEucor – The European Campus brings together five universities in the border region between Germany, France, and Switzerland. Eucor encourages exchanges and the sharing of expertise between students, researchers, and staff at member universities.\nInternational Credit Mobility (ICM)\nInternational Credit Mobility (ICM) supports the internationalisation of higher education institutions. This programme enables students, doctoral candidates and higher education staff to undertake short-term mobility between Erasmus+ programme countries and partner countries. The objectives are to foster professional development, increase employability, and acquire new teaching methods.\nMenu\nBrowse those links to navigate the website\nDisplay\nHide\nthe searchbox\nFill in your search :\nLaunch search\nClose\nOur audiences :\nStudent Profile\nResearcher Profile\nI think about it\nBefore\nmy arrival\nI am\nin\nStrasbourg\nBefore\nmy departure\nServices Pack"
  ],
